      "description": "## Overview\n[std/net/http](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http) is a Go standard library package std/net/http\n\nAffected versions of this package are vulnerable to Insertion of Sensitive Information Into Sent Data. <br><br>**Go Vulnerability Report:**<br>\r\nThe HTTP client drops sensitive headers after following a cross-domain redirect. For example, a request to a.com/ containing an Authorization header which is redirected to b.com/ will not send that header to b.com.In the event that the client received a subsequent same-domain redirect, however, the sensitive headers would be restored. For example, a chain of redirects from a.com/, to b.com/1, and finally to b.com/2 would incorrectly send the Authorization header to b.com/2.\n## Remediation\nUpgrade `std/net/http` to version 1.22.11, 1.23.5, 1.24.0-rc.2 or higher.\n## References\n- [Go Advisory](https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2025-3420)\n- [Go Commit](https://go.dev/cl/643100)\n- [Go Issue](https://go.dev/issue/70530)\n- [Google Groups Forum](https://groups.google.com/g/golang-dev/c/bG8cv1muIBM/m/G461hA6lCgAJ)\n- [Google Groups Forum](https://groups.google.com/g/golang-dev/c/CAWXhan3Jww/m/bk9LAa-lCgAJ)\n",
